   "source": [
    "## What is Parallel Computing?\n",
    "\n",
    "Parallel computing involves breaking down a large task into smaller subtasks that can be executed simultaneously across multiple processors or cores."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from multiprocessing import Pool\n",
    "import time\n",
    "\n",
    "# Simple parallel computing example\n",
    "def square(x):\n",
    "    return x ** 2\n",
    "\n",
    "if __name__ == '__main__':\n",
    "    numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n",
    "    with Pool(4) as p:\n",
    "        results = p.map(square, numbers)\n",
    "    print(f'Results: {results}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Key Benefits\n",
    "\n",
    "- Faster execution time\n",
